This is what I get for trying to be too clever.

It's been aaaages since I played Nethack. About 7-8 years back I
ascended a Wizard and a Valkyrie, but I'm very rusty now after a long
break, so my characters aren't really getting past the early game at
the moment. This is a prime example of how dangerous my sketchy memory
can be for my characters.

On my current excursion with a Rogue, things are generally looking
rather promising. I Ditched my shortsword straight off and relied
entirely on my 12 daggers. Reached level 6 in hte main donugeon before
I felt ready to enter the mines.

Minetown had a co-aligned altar, and I'd found plenty of food on the
way, so I decided to take things slowly, build up a stash there and
completely clear the first 3 mine levels of equipment. A quick bit of
price identification confirmed that the lamp I'd found in the mines
was blessed and magic, but I was unable to decide on what to wish for,
so I kept it as a permanent light-source for the time being.

By the time I'd finished building up my stash, I was level 10.
Sacrificing at the altar gave me Sting (I was annoyed at first, as I
usually name Sting as soon as I find an Elven dagger, but as I was
using daggers as primary weapons anyway, it actually served me very
well). Later, I sacrificed some more and got Frost Brand (nice!).

Took out the captain of the guard by setting a bear trap and throwing
daggers at him. Between Frost Brand and his silver sabre, I now own
the h2h weapons I'll be using in late game (should I survive that
for).

So generally, things look peachy, except for one thing. And this is
where the sketchy memory threw a spanner in the works.

I killed a tengu, and somewhere in the reaches of my memory, a little
voice reminded me, "teleport control". Great! I thought, and yummed it
up.

"You feel very jumpy!"

Crap! I forgot about that possibility. After a level or two with
teleportitis, I started to remember how annoying and potentially
dangerous it could be. But I wasn't to be beaten.

I #rubbed my magic lamp, and when a djinni appeared, I asked him for 2
cursed scrolls of genocide (having no blank scrolls, and not wanting
to waste good ones for paper). I read the first, asked for Tengus and
slaughtered the lot. But alas! I ate 4 corpses and none conferred
teleport control.

Oh well, one more scroll. Wash, rinse, repeat. This time only one
corpse was left behind. No teleport control.

Gah! Why didn't I just ask for a ring of teleport control!? It's not
like food was scarse!

Now I'm going to traipse back to my minetown stash to see if one of my
un-id'd rings is tele control. Maybe I'll find one in Sokoban. The
Master Key confers tele control iirc but I haven't reached the quest
level yet, and I have 4 levels to gain before I can start it (last one
needs to come from a wraith corpse or potion of gain experience iirc).

It's not dwypi, but it's really annoying. I've obviously got to
relearn all those lessons of caution I first learnt nearly 10 years
ago...


